WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.380
In a hymn of the Rig Veda, the gods offer
up a cosmic Person in a great sacrifice.

2
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:10.470
From his body the world is
made: the moon from his mind,

3
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.470
the sun from his eye.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.960
And from his mouth, arms, thighs and
feet come four classes of people.

5
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.000
So does this ancient
hymn make caste sacred?

6
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:25.730
In this mission, you'll meet the
four varnas and their duties,

7
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.400
and ask whether class comes
by birth or by nature.

8
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:34.150
Then you'll ask what this picture of
one body could mean for Hindus today.

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:39.000
Your mission: weigh up whether this
ancient hymn makes caste sacred.
